      "dom_id": "step-q121321",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "A man on a boat is sailing towards a $247\\,\\text{ft}$ high lighthouse. If the height of the man above the sea is $10\\,\\text{ft},$ how fast is the man approaching the lighthouse if his shadow is shrinking at a rate of $0.25\\,\\text{mi/h}?$ Round your answer to one decimal place.",
      "worked_solution": "Let's draw a figure according to the given data.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14209554/assets/6c85e0c34b34dd9dcb384bb601b9b87a1a6b7174888c9ad49d8c2cd37abc13de.png)\n\nIn the figure, $x$ is the distance from the man to the lighthouse, while $y$ is the length of his shadow. Both $x$ and $y$ change with time. In particular, we know that the man's shadow's velocity is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=-0.25\\,\\text{mi/h}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the man's shadow's velocity is *negative* because he is walking *toward* the lighthouse, and therefore the distance between him and the lighthouse *decreases* with time.\n\nSince we want to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},$ we need to find a relation between $x$ and $y.$ Since the two triangles are similar, the ratios between the corresponding sides are equal, and we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+y}{247} & =\\frac{y}{10} \\\\ 10x+10y & =247y \\\\ 10x & =237y \\\\ x & =23.7y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe differentiate both sides of the above equation with respect to $t$ using the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(23.7y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =23.7\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=-0.25\\,\\text{mi/h}$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =23.7(-0.25)≈-5.9\\,\\text{mi/h}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto one decimal place.\n\nTherefore, the man's speed is approximately $5.9\\,\\text{mi/h}.$",
